    "title": "New Orleans used to host competitive baseball all the time — then Katrina hit",
    "text": "As New Orleans prepares to host the Savannah Bananas at the Caesars Superdome this weekend, WDSU is taking a look back at when the Dome hosted competitive baseball. The Savannah Bananas games will be held Saturday, March 14, at 6 p.m. and Sunday, March 15, at 3 p.m.The Dome used to host college and professional competitive baseball games all the time until Katrina hit. Once the Dome was renovated, the space could no longer accommodate competitive baseball games. When the Savannah Bananas face the Party Animals this weekend, it will be the first time a competitive baseball game has been played in the Dome since 2004. WDSU looked into our archives to find footage of competitive baseball at the Dome prior to the storm. We found a video of the Oakland A's playing the New York Mets in a Major League Baseball spring training exhibition in March 1992. Watch the video in the player above. For more on the Savannah Bananas games, click here. NEW ORLEANS —As New Orleans prepares to host the Savannah Bananas at the Caesars Superdome this weekend, WDSU is taking a look back at when the Dome hosted competitive baseball. The Savannah Bananas games will be held Saturday, March 14, at 6 p.m. and Sunday, March 15, at 3 p.m. The Dome used to host college and professional competitive baseball games all the time until Katrina hit. Once the Dome was renovated, the space could no longer accommodate competitive baseball games. When the Savannah Bananas face the Party Animals this weekend, it will be the first time a competitive baseball game has been played in the Dome since 2004. WDSU looked into our archives to find footage of competitive baseball at the Dome prior to the storm. Video Player is loading.Current Time 0:00Duration 0:00Remaining Time 0:00 We found a video of the Oakland A's playing the New York Mets in a Major League Baseball spring training exhibition in March 1992. Watch the video in the player above. For more on the Savannah Bananas games, click here.",
